  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Hospitals, clinics and families pay for safe, reliable care. They judge you by safety record, documentation and how you treat people.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is double-checking identity and instructions before any task.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and skills for nursing careers: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools help with scheduling, notes and learning. Routine documentation tasks shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Bedside judgment, compassion and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn and organise; later, own patient care within your role.
  </p>

